@@ # raf-remaster line script for the stock 'unit functions.fx'.
@@ # Lines starting with '@@ ' reference the player's stock file; all other lines are ours.
@@ # Made by tools/make_shader_patch.py, applied by tools/build_shaders.py.
@@ drop 4 6b19f659
/*
 * Unit Functions.fx  (raf-remaster rewrite; replaces the stock file)
 *
 * Same entry points as stock (VS_NormalModel, VS_ShadowMapModel, VS_ZOnlyModel,
 * PS_NormalModel, PS_HighlightModel) and the same effect parameters. What
 * changed is the math:
 *   - lighting (light cube or the half-lambert fallback) runs per pixel for
 *     every unit, not only normal-mapped ones;
 *   - normal maps use a tangent frame that is skinned with the bones;
 *   - Blinn-Phong specular per pixel, masked like stock where the material
 *     has a mask, with a small default where it has none;
 *   - a gentle rim light on every unit (stock rim only on rim-flagged ones);
 *   - specular and rim are added in linear light; the base colour, including
 *     the team colour, is computed exactly as stock.
 * Position math is shared by all vertex shaders so the z-only pass and the
 * colour pass of "accurate opacity" produce identical depth (ZFunc EQUAL).
 */

@@ keep 1 1742b230
